+## Proposed amendment RC0-E0-001 — requires Cox ratification
+
+One optional `ai_mode` in the existing instance config selects `hosted` (omitted default) or `off`; no alternate file, environment fallback, parser or CLI. Rerank requests default false; Stage 1 has no admitted rerank provider, so explicit requests remain truthfully unavailable. `embedding` and the API provider handle are required only when hosted; OFF permits both to be absent and also allows retaining valid BOUND metadata/opaque references, so the single switch suffices; retained fields are never selected or resolved, and a GAP is not a dummy OFF identity. OFF keeps all non-AI original-owner, Core/C04, resolver, native, SQL-role, transport and enrollment requirements. The local extractor identity names existing graph facts and is not a hosted credential or embedding dependency.
+
+`secret_handles_by_mode.api` is the common three-handle view. Hosted API admission appends exactly `ai_policy.hosted_api_handle`; OFF does not. Other process views stay exact. RC2 derives one immutable AI selection only after full existing admission: admission identity is SHA-256 of the exact admitted config bytes, not an execution grant. The current gate revision must additionally have a non-reusable boot/acceptance epoch, or reject reused revisions, so ON/OFF/identical-ON cannot revalidate old work. There is no environment or request override of OFF.
+
+The sole embedding destination is HTTPS origin `https://openrouter.ai:443`, exact path `/api/v1/embeddings`, POST only; disable redirects and environment proxies. Match the entire admitted current embedding tuple before key/cache/HTTP work. Use the existing purpose-bound opaque provider reference and resolver, one API-lifetime bounded HTTP client, no SDK, model daemon or secret store. Hosted default does not supply owner data/spend authority.
+
+An accepted installation OFF revision stops new AI dispatch before acknowledgement, cancels in-flight work and fences/drops late output before cache/vector/publication or response. No provider resolver, HTTP, semantic cache read/write, vector search, document queue/enqueue/retry or rerank may start after that revision; warm vectors do not bypass OFF. Previously sent text cannot be recalled. Stored vectors are retained; re-enable requires full admission/current scope and never schedules bulk catch-up implicitly.
+
+Keep one absolute monotonic request deadline from HTTP admission through auth, waits, resolver, cache, provider and final checks, clamped to the existing `budgets.request_ms` (10000); subordinate limits only shorten it. OFF search uses bounded current-authorized canonical keyword reads and preserves the separate graph read with actual freshness. Unsupported kinds/payloads and scan bounds are typed, never successful silent empty/complete. Any C11 response ABI change requires Cox approval.
+
+This amendment changes declarations only. Its diff is not applied by E0. After ratification, Cox must re-freeze operations.expected/paired fixture digests and original member descriptors, and coordinate the exact config/operations byte pins with E1/RC2. Old pins must continue refusing changed bytes until that explicit coordinated update; do not add multi-revision fallback. Every earlier frozen test source remains unchanged and must pass with E1. Production R01/Core/native/effect authority is still UNBOUND. E3 and DEP-W projection writers remain separate scope.
